+The acceptance suite (real browser / Cypress) reports 5 failures, all from the same root cause: the `render()` function in `js/app.js` replaces `todoListEl.innerHTML` and `todoCountEl.innerHTML` on every state change. This destroys and recreates DOM nodes, detaching any references a real browser held before the interaction. Cypress cannot `cy.eq()` or `cy.find()` on detached elements.
 
-Updated `watchbill.json` with `watch1` naming the new scenario, shifting the existing watches to 2-10.
+The in-harness suite (happy-dom) does not reproduce this because it re-queries the DOM for every assertion, never holding stale references. The defects are real: a real browser fails on:
